<title>EGYPT: Egypt money supply up 13.7 pct in yr to end April.</title>
<headline>Egypt money supply up 13.7 pct in yr to end April.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egyptian broad money supply grew 13.7 percent in the year ending April 1997, from 13.3 percent in the year to March 1997, the Central Bank of Egypt said in a bulletin available on Monday.</p>
<p>Total money supply, including quasi-money and foreign currency deposits, was 187.380 billion pounds at end-April 1997 against 183.942 billion at end-March.</p>
<p>Following figures, in billions of pounds, were supplied by the Central Bank.</p>
<p>					 April 97  March 97    April 96</p>
<p>    Total money supply	   187.380   183.942*   164.818</p>
<p>    Money			     38.593    37.722*    34.811</p>
<p>    Quasi-money		    148.787   146.220*   130.007</p>
<p>    Year-on-year growth (pct)   +13.7     +13.3	 --</p>
<p>    Month-on-month growth (pct) +1.86     +0.72	1.87</p>
<p>* Amended by the Central Bank.</p>
<p>$1 = 3.395 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
